WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.510
Ben watched in horror as the skinny cat dashed around spectators' legs and darted under chairs.

2
00:00:06.511 --> 00:00:12.798
A big mouse monster stood on his chair. "Eek! A cat!"

3
00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:16.725
"Woof! Woof!" Rex-Rex ran after the cat.

4
00:00:16.726 --> 00:00:22.787
The frightened cat streaked toward Mrs. Hubbletree, who was clutching Bowie protectively to her chest.

5
00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:27.064
The gecko rapidly changed colors to match her colorful dress.

6
00:00:27.065 --> 00:00:32.336
"Watch out, dear! I'll protect you!" Mayor Hubbletree pushed his wife out of the way.

7
00:00:32.337 --> 00:00:36.702
He tripped over the cat and fell on his face. "Ouch!"

8
00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:41.354
"I'm sorry!" Mog yelled, chasing his dog.

9
00:00:41.355 --> 00:00:46.414
"I'm sorry too!" the cat owner shouted, racing after Mog and the pets. "I

10
00:00:46.415 --> 00:00:50.373
hope this won't affect my score in the obedience contest!" Ben

11
00:00:50.374 --> 00:00:54.774
could hear Miss Bungle making frantic announcements into the microphone. But

12
00:00:54.775 --> 00:00:56.544
no one was listening. Then—

13
00:00:56.545 --> 00:01:04.159
wham! Rex-Rex crashed into Deb, causing her piranha-keet cage to fly into the air.

14
00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.041
More cages crashed to the floor.

15
00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:11.886
Mr. Freaky jumped out of the way, his noses wiggling. "Ahh!"

16
00:01:11.887 --> 00:01:17.487
"Wrawk! Everything is totally out of control!" Deb’s piranha-keet squawked.

17
00:01:17.488 --> 00:01:20.832
The cat and dog ran around and around.

18
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:25.695
Near the pet adoption booth, the skinny cat's owner abruptly halted.

19
00:01:25.696 --> 00:01:28.575
"Kitty!" she shouted. "Come here now!"

20
00:01:28.576 --> 00:01:36.291
"No!" Samantha stood at the booth, holding a ferret with one hand while she held a skeleton dog's leash with the other.

21
00:01:36.292 --> 00:01:37.478
"Please don't—"

22
00:01:37.479 --> 00:01:39.014
But it was too late.

23
00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:42.462
The skinny cat turned and flew at her owner.

24
00:01:42.463 --> 00:01:47.268
But Rex-Rex was still running straight ahead, and—

25
00:01:47.269 --> 00:01:49.607
crash! He slammed into the

26
00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:54.141
booth. Ben gasped as the adoption booth toppled

27
00:01:54.142 --> 00:01:56.382
over. "Whoa!" Mog

28
00:01:56.383 --> 00:02:01.003
said. He called for his dog, who was sniffing around in the stuff from the

29
00:02:01.004 --> 00:02:02.988
booth. "Rex-Rex,

30
00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:06.310
come!" Rex-Rex obediently trotted over to

31
00:02:06.311 --> 00:02:09.693
Mog. "Look, he found a toy!" Sid said.

32
00:02:09.694 --> 00:02:14.521
"Good," Mog said. "Maybe he'll forget about that dumb cat."

33
00:02:14.522 --> 00:02:16.534
Ben grabbed his brother's arm.

34
00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:20.552
"Come on, Sid. Let's see if we can help Samantha fix the pet adoption booth."

35
00:02:20.553 --> 00:02:24.713
But before they could move, Samantha hurried toward them.

36
00:02:24.714 --> 00:02:29.936
"Excuse me, Mog. That toy belongs to the skeleton dog." She smiled.

37
00:02:29.937 --> 00:02:33.216
"He's an orphan, and that's his only possession."

38
00:02:33.217 --> 00:02:39.851
"Aw. Sorry about that." Mog got the toy from Rex-Rex and handed it over.

39
00:02:39.852 --> 00:02:45.526
"Thanks," Samantha said with a sigh. "What a crazy chase, huh?"

40
00:02:45.527 --> 00:02:48.421
"We can help you fix the booth," Ben said.

41
00:02:48.422 --> 00:02:52.088
Her eyes lit up. "Thank you!"

42
00:02:52.089 --> 00:02:56.659
*** It took a short time for Ben to help Samantha set up the adoption booth

43
00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:01.712
again. Sid held the ferret and the skeleton dog's leash while Ben

44
00:03:01.713 --> 00:03:07.581
worked. Soon they were back in their seats with Winnie, waiting for the obedience show to

45
00:03:07.582 --> 00:03:12.018
continue. "This is more like a disobedience show," Sid

46
00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:20.171
said. Ben laughed. "Are you itchy?" he asked, noticing some fresh green

47
00:03:20.172 --> 00:03:23.087
spots. "Nah. I'm fine. Look!" Sid

48
00:03:23.088 --> 00:03:25.832
added. "Waldo and Oswald are about to take their

49
00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:29.590
turn." They watched as Waldo demonstrated what his owl could do.

50
00:03:29.591 --> 00:03:35.554
For once, the owl behaved, following all of Waldo's commands.

51
00:03:35.555 --> 00:03:39.230
Waldo looked proud when he came over with his owl.

52
00:03:39.231 --> 00:03:43.538
"We killed it!" Waldo whispered. "We did so great!"

53
00:03:43.539 --> 00:03:47.170
"Um, Waldo . . . " Winnie held Inky tightly.

54
00:03:47.171 --> 00:03:51.539
"Do me a favor and don't mention killing around Oswald, okay?

55
00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.464
He might notice the tasty meal that's sitting on my lap right now."

56
00:03:55.465 --> 00:04:02.153
After the judges talked quietly for a few minutes, Miss Bungle announced the obedience contest winner.

57
00:04:02.154 --> 00:04:09.717
It was a spider who could spin fancy webs on command.

58
00:04:09.718 --> 00:04:12.781
"Too bad, guys," Ben said to his friends.

59
00:04:12.782 --> 00:04:15.233
"I thought one of your pets would win."

60
00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:20.217
Mog shrugged. "I entered Rex-Rex in the best pet competition too.

61
00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:23.282
Maybe we'll do well in that one." He grinned.

62
00:04:23.283 --> 00:04:26.485
"I think he's twice as good as any other pet here."

63
00:04:26.486 --> 00:04:30.438
"No way!" Winnie joked. "Inky is the best pet."

64
00:04:30.439 --> 00:04:33.372
"Nope, it's Oswald!" Waldo chimed in.

65
00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:37.704
As the others talked about their pets, Ben saw Sid look down.

66
00:04:37.705 --> 00:04:40.316
Ben couldn't help feeling bad too.

67
00:04:40.317 --> 00:04:43.180
"Will we ever find a pet?" he thought.

68
00:04:43.181 --> 00:04:46.577
It sure didn't seem likely.

69
00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:53.270
*** Ben and Sid finished their volunteer duties and then returned to the stage area to watch the final event.

70
00:04:53.271 --> 00:05:02.166
The room seemed to crackle with excitement—even the zombies were watching the stage alertly, ready to witness the best pets perform.

71
00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:05.245
"This is so exciting!" Winnie said.

72
00:05:05.246 --> 00:05:09.307
As Ben turned to smile at her, Inky let out a hiss.

73
00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:14.964
Ben rolled his eyes. "Not again, Inky. This cat really hates me."

74
00:05:14.965 --> 00:05:19.166
"I don't think she hates you," Winnie began. "She just doesn't—"

75
00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:23.649
"Oh no!" A startled shriek rang out inside the gym.

76
00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:29.062
"Ahh! Bowie is gone!"

